    <version>28.3.2</version>
    <authors>Joe Armstrong,Robert Virding,Mike Williams</authors>
    <owners>Luke Bakken, Team RabbitMQ</owners>
    <summary>Erlang/OTP - for building concurrent, distributed, and fault tolerant systems</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[**OTP** is a set of Erlang libraries, which consists of the Erlang runtime system, a number of ready-to-use components mainly written in Erlang, and a set of design principles for Erlang programs.

## Features

* **Concurrency** - Lightweight processes with message passing
* **Distribution** - Built-in support for distributed systems
* **Fault Tolerance** - Supervision trees and hot code swapping
* **Soft Real-Time** - Predictable low-latency response times
* **High Availability** - Design for systems that never stop

## Use Cases

Erlang is used in telecoms, banking, e-commerce, instant messaging, and any system requiring high availability and scalability.

Learn more at [erlang.org](https://www.erlang.org).
]]></description>
